      "heading": "B - Audience, Right-of-way",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B - Audience, Right-of-way\n\nThe audience is first-time never-licensed applicants preparing for the regular passenger-car written knowledge test, reading at a plain-English level. This section teaches interaction judgment only: who goes first at crossings, how to answer emergency vehicles, circling roundabouts, and changing lanes and passing safely. It assumes no prior driving knowledge and carries no prerequisites beyond literacy. Readers must make split-second priority calls, so wording stays scenario-driven and concrete throughout.\n",
